course: dictionary
lesson: 3338
title: What is evolution?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Evolution is how living things change over a very long time, from one generation to the next. A generation is one step in a family, like parents and then their children.
explain: Evolution does not mean getting better in general. «A fish is not worse than a person, it is fitted to water.» A living thing changes so that it fits the place where it lives, and if that place changes, the best fit changes too.
explain: The word can also mean the slow change and development of anything. When people talk about «the evolution of phones», they mean how phones have changed step by step over time, each new one a small change from the one before.
fact: Evolution means living things change over a very long time, from one generation to the next.
fact: The picture of a line of apes turning into a man is misleading, because evolution is a branching bush, not a ladder.
fact: Many human relatives lived at the same time, so evolution has many branches.
fact: Evolution is supported by fossils, by DNA and by changes we can watch happening today.
fact: Evolution can also mean the slow change and development of anything, such as phones or cars.
exercise: What does evolution mean for living things? | Growing bigger in one day | Moving to a new house | Staying the same forever | *Change over a very long time, from one generation to the next
exercise: «Evolution is a branching bush, not a ladder.» What does the bush show? | A single fish in water | A straight line going up, with each step better than the last | A tree that never grows | *Many branches, with different relatives living at the same time
exercise: Which of these supports evolution? | A feeling about the weather | *Fossils | Nothing at all, it is only a story | A rule that nobody can check
test: Why is a fish not worse than a person in evolution? | Because it lives on land | Because it is the newest animal | *Because it is fitted to the water where it lives | Because it can breathe air like a person
test: Which picture best shows evolution? | A ladder going straight up | A single straight line | *A branching bush | A circle with no ends
exam: Why is a line of apes turning into a man a misleading picture of evolution? | Because humans came first, before every other animal | *Because evolution is a branching bush, not a ladder, with many relatives living at the same time | Because apes never change | Because it shows a fish
